# The daily audit archive (issue #1296).
#
# AUDIT_ARCHIVE_URI is the key prefix every archived day is written under,
# inside the composed object-storage service's own bucket. Unset means no
# archive is configured: nothing is scheduled, no worker runs, and the audit
# log's only copy is the database table — which is the state this key exists to
# leave.
#
# It names a PREFIX and never a bucket. The object-storage service's write
# carries no bucket, so the bucket, its credentials and its retention policy
# belong to the composition that points that service at one; a value naming a
# bucket, a host or a scheme (`s3://…`) fails the boot rather than writing
# somewhere the operator did not choose.
#
#   (unset)              — no archive.
#   audit/archive        — <bucket>/audit/archive/YYYY/MM/DD/audit-YYYY-MM-DD.json
#
# The object is written create-if-absent, so an archived day's bytes cannot be
# replaced by a later run, and each day's receipt — key, digest, byte and event
# counts — is recorded in the audit log itself. That makes the archive
# tamper-EVIDENT. Making it tamper-PROOF needs an object-lock/retention policy
# on the bucket, which belongs to the infrastructure that provisions it; see
# module/AUDIT_METRICS.md.
#
# Unset on this profile: a developer's local object store is not an archive.
AUDIT_ARCHIVE_URI=
